@startuml
' Source block: uml251_10_timing (uml-2.5.1-legend.puml intake)
!include ../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/interaction/timing-diagram-style.iuml
' ============================================================================
' Section 10 — Timing Diagrams
'
' UML traceability:
'   UML 2.5.1 §17.11 Timing Diagrams
'   UML 2.5.1 §8.4 Time / §8.5 Intervals
'
' PlantUML support: Native/Partial.
' ============================================================================

title UML 2.5.1 Notation Reference — Timing Diagrams
skinparam monochrome true

robust "Controller" as Controller
concise "Mode" as Mode
binary "ready" as Ready

@0
Controller is Idle
Mode is Off
Ready is low

@100
Controller -> Mode : start
Controller is Processing
Mode is Starting

@200
Mode is Active
Ready is high

@350
Mode -> Controller : complete
Controller is Waiting

@500
Controller is Idle
Mode is Off
Ready is low

Controller@100 <-> @200 : {100 ms startup}
@200 <-> @350 : {150 ms active interval}

note bottom of Mode
  UML Timing Diagrams show Lifelines whose state/value changes
  are positioned against a time axis. Timing and duration
  constraints constrain observations or intervals.

  PlantUML robust/concise/binary/clock are renderer-specific
  timing representations that map well to common UML timing views.
end note

legend
  |= UML concept |= PlantUML mapping |
  | Lifeline | robust / concise / binary / clock participant |
  | State/value | "Participant is Value" |
  | State change | @time + value assignment |
  | Message | timed participant arrow |
  | Time axis | @time / scale / axis controls |
  | Timing / duration constraint | anchor/time <-> anchor/time : {constraint} |
endlegend
@enduml
